SUMMARY:6th Annual Miller Summer Mixtape at Miller Outdoor Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Miller Outdoor Theatre presents the sixth annual Miller Summer Mixtape\, a showcase of how HTX is anything but a single genre\, hosted by Houston music icon Kam Franklin. \nFor 2026\, the lineup highlights Houston’s unique rich musical tapestry\, from the soulful storytelling of Sara Van Buskirk\, to the blues-infused rock of Saint Judas and The Black Hymns\, to the powerhouse vocals of Rodell Duff. \nDJ Mikey Drag will also spin a genre-spanning mix of country classics\, twangy favorites\, and a little cumbia fuego. \nFinding Your Seat at Miller Outdoor Theatre\nAs always\, all seats at Miller are free\, but covered seating for popular evening shows usually requires a free assigned ticket reserved 24 hours in advance. \nLearn more about getting free seated tickets at Miller. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more or reserve a free seated ticket. \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details.  \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/miller-summer-mixtape-at-miller-outdoor-theatre-2026/
LOCATION:Miller Outdoor Theatre\, 6000 Hermann Park Dr\, Houston\, TX\, 77030\, United States
