SUMMARY:Incredible India: Call of the Flute at Miller Outdoor Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Miller Outdoor Theatre welcomes Indian Performing Arts Samskriti\, in collaboration with the Consulate General of India\, Houston\, in a live performance of Incredible India: Call of the Flute on view for free under the stars in Hermann Park. \nArtists from Houston\, Austin and Dallas enact stories of Krishna in dance and music. And as the dance gathers momentum\, music fills the air\, magical\, celestial\, divine\, ethereal\, as Krishna plays. \nFinding Your Seat at Miller Outdoor Theatre \nAs always\, all seats at Miller are free\, but covered seating for popular evening shows usually requires a free assigned ticket reserved 24 hours in advance. \nLearn more about getting free seated tickets at Miller. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more or reserve a free seated ticket. \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details.  \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/incredible-india-call-of-the-flute-at-miller-outdoor-theatre/
